WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:04.140
"She-Hulk" smashed it with all&nbsp;
those cool cameos in Season 1,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.140 --> 00:00:08.880
but the final guest spot might just&nbsp;
be the most exciting. Here's why.

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:12.540
Season 1 of "She-Hulk: Attorney at&nbsp;
Law" featured several appearances&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.540 --> 00:00:17.760
from characters across the Marvel Cinematic&nbsp;
Universe, from The Hulk to Wong to Daredevil.

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:22.200
"I just wanna make sure that you don't think this&nbsp;
is one of those 'cameo every week' type of shows."

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:25.320
That hasn't been something that fans&nbsp;
have been complaining about, though,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:30.240
as many tuned in to "She-Hulk" specifically to&nbsp;
see Daredevil in action, since his appearance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:35.340
was teased in an early trailer for the show.&nbsp;
Entire threads on the Marvel Studios subreddit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:40.140
were dedicated to discussing when "The&nbsp;
Man Without Fear" would finally show up.

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:44.460
In a Marvel.com interview with the show's&nbsp;
creator, Jessica Gao, she talked about how&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.460 --> 00:00:48.420
thrilled she was to be allowed to use&nbsp;
a character like Daredevil. After all,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:53.220
Matt Murdock is no stranger to the courtroom&nbsp;
or the superhero lifestyle. Gao explained,

00:00:53.220 --> 00:00:59.280
"It just made so much sense that he would be on&nbsp;
this show because both he and Jen are lawyers by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:03.840
day, Super Heroes outside of the office,&nbsp;
even though Jen is doing it reluctantly.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:08.340
What better character to kind of show how&nbsp;
this struggle she's having is possible?"

00:01:08.340 --> 00:01:12.060
But, while Daredevil may have been&nbsp;
the focus of many fans' attention,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.060 --> 00:01:15.480
the character casually introduced&nbsp;
at the end of the "She-Hulk:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.480 --> 00:01:18.960
Attorney at Law" Season 1 finale&nbsp;
might be an even bigger deal.

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:21.600
At the end of the finale, Jen Walters, her family,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:26.640
and Matt Murdock relish in the defeat of the&nbsp;
conniving Intelligencia group. Unexpectedly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:32.460
Bruce Banner — who spent much of the series&nbsp;
in space for unknown reasons — shows up at the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.460 --> 00:01:39.240
family barbecue to introduce his son, Skaar. He&nbsp;
appears only briefly and doesn't have any lines,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:44.100
but it still opens the door for this character&nbsp;
to enter the Marvel Cinematic Universe.

00:01:44.100 --> 00:01:49.440
In the comics, Skaar was canonically introduced&nbsp;
in "World War Hulk" #5 as part of the plotline&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.440 --> 00:01:54.000
where Hulk was banished to the planet of&nbsp;
Sakaar. Hulk conceived Skaar with Caiera&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:59.340
the Oldstrong and the child matured very&nbsp;
quickly, becoming a teen in just one year.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.340 --> 00:02:04.440
In addition to having his father's powers,&nbsp;
Skaar also has his mother's abilities known&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.440 --> 00:02:09.600
as "Old Powers" which include being able&nbsp;
to control and manipulate the earth itself.

00:02:09.600 --> 00:02:13.020
It's notable that Hulk has already&nbsp;
spent time on Sakaar in the MCU,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.020 --> 00:02:17.280
after Thor found him there where he had&nbsp;
been spending years in Hulk form fighting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:21.480
in tournaments held by the Grandmaster.&nbsp;
Not much is explained in the brief scene&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.480 --> 00:02:25.440
introducing Skaar, but Bruce says he&nbsp;
made a return trip to the trash planet.

00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:28.440
"I know I've been away on Sakaar for awhile."

00:02:28.440 --> 00:02:32.520
Fans on Reddit were already excited&nbsp;
about the opportunities that Skaar's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.520 --> 00:02:34.800
introduction makes possible. One posted,

00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:40.320
"I just hope we'll know more about what happened&nbsp;
to Bruce on Sakaar in another serie[s]/movie."

00:02:40.320 --> 00:02:44.280
Others shared concerns about the&nbsp;
character's design, with one fan posting,

00:02:44.280 --> 00:02:49.080
"Can I just say that Skaar looks...&nbsp;
off. Not referring to CGI, just,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.080 --> 00:02:54.300
doesn't look like Skaar and looks like a&nbsp;
Hulked up space teen and not the warrior."

00:02:54.300 --> 00:02:58.260
If Marvel decides to redesign the&nbsp;
character for future appearances,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.260 --> 00:03:00.720
it would hardly be the first time that happened.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.720 --> 00:03:05.160
But, misgivings aside, it's likely that&nbsp;
Skaar will appear again in the near future.

